  "body": "## What changed\n\n- A welded smooth face (`FeatureSel::Patch`) can now be a cavity wall in \"electrode from faces\".\n- The app expands the patch into its planar strips (`feature::patches`). Each strip is read like a planar pick (`sinker_faces::faces_of`).\n- The new motion rule `sinker_cavity::welded_wall` checks each strip. Every strip must be a vertical plane.\n- `cavity_of` then stands each strip on the floor ring, like any wall. Its other refusals apply to each strip.\n- A strip that leans, or that is level, refuses the whole welded face. The message names the welded face and the strip.\n- A stale patch id is refused with \"no longer in the model: re-pick it\".\n\n## Cause\n\n`face_of` returned a blank face marked `curved` for each patch pick. `check_face` then refused it as \"a curved wall\". The tangent wall band of a rounded-corner pocket welds into one patch. So a click on a rounded corner gave a pick that could not make an electrode.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `sinker_electrode_body::a_rounded_pockets_corners_picked_as_welded_faces_yield_the_strips_electrode` (new). The floor and the one welded face (20 strips: four flat walls and sixteen corner strips) give the same electrode as the planar-strip pick. The finish burn is judged clean. The welded face picked beside its own strips gives the same electrode. A stale patch is refused by name.\n  - Red before the fix: \"welded face 0xe26b11036b29702e of 'part' is a curved wall - an electrode is generated from planar walls only\".\n- `sinker_electrode_tests::a_welded_wall_is_read_strip_by_strip_and_a_leaning_strip_is_refused_by_name` (new, motion unit test). Two vertical strips read as the planar wall. A strip drafted 4.764 degrees is refused by name. A level strip and an empty weld are refused by name.\n- `sinker_electrode::a_rounded_pockets_corner_picked_as_its_welded_face_is_refused_by_name` is now `..._reads_as_its_strips`. This change intentionally reverses its old expectation. It now asserts the same electrode as the planar pick.\n\nMutation checks:\n- Old `sinker_faces.rs` put back: the app pins fail (red). Fix restored: they pass (green).\n- The vertical guard in `welded_wall` disabled: the motion pin fails (red). Guard restored: it passes (green).\n\nGate: `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` is green (motion lib, app lib, `sinker_electrode`, `sinker_electrode_body`, `sinker_electrode_mcp`). `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` is clean.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. No posted G-code changes.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- A real model from a CAD import with a welded wall. The fixture is a synthetic mesh built in code.\n- A drafted or blended curved wall. It stays refused by name; a lofted electrode is not modelled.\n- Not exercised on a real EDM control. Synthetic conditions only.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nNone in the changed functions. #1738 lists `crates/app/src/operation/sinker_faces.rs` only because its base branch is stale. Against upstream/main it does not change that file. #1753 does not change these files.\n\nDecision record: `docs/decisions/1808-welded-walls.md`.\n\nChangelog: Sinker EDM: \"electrode from faces\" accepts a rounded-corner wall picked as its welded face; a welded wall that leans is refused by name (#1808)\n\nFixes #1808\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
